{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01836zBAzhLStgdRcToJgDMv","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"f16e56d46cd2f0be72baa4d3863328c1f67b1155\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T22:52:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Keep the subscription form and report the error when saving fails (#417)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Keep the subscription form and report the error when saving fails\\n\\nSaving the OCL subscription wrote the new values into the SWR cache\\noptimistically, then checked `response.ok`. `openmrsFetch` rejects on any\\nnon-2xx response, so the error branch was unreachable, and the optimistic\\nwrite stored a bare subscription where `useSubscription` expects\\n`{ data: { results: [...] } }`. On a failed save the hook read\\n`undefined`, the effect cleared every input, no revalidation ran, and the\\nonly feedback was the framework's generic unhandled-error toast.\\n\\nDrop the optimistic write and wrap the save in try/catch. On failure,\\nshow the app's own error notification with the server message and leave\\nthe inputs as typed. On success, revalidate and show the existing success\\nmessage.\\n\\nAlso judge an import upload by its `.zip` extension rather than its MIME\\ntype. Browsers report ZIPs as any of the four types the backend accepts,\\nor with no type at all, so the old check rejected valid archives on some\\nplatforms, while accepting `application/octet-stream` alone would have\\nlet any unknown binary through with a message saying only .zip files are\\nallowed.\\n\\n* Show the backend's reason when saving the subscription fails\\n\\nThe error notification repeated `openmrsFetch`'s generic \\\"Server\\nresponded with 500\\\" message. The backend puts its reason in the response\\nbody, so show that when it is there and fall back to the fetch error\\notherwise.\\n\\n* Accept uploads by extension only and guard an empty drop\\n\\nCarbon's drop container already matches `.zip` by extension and never\\ndiscards a file for a MIME mismatch, so the MIME list only widened the\\nnative file picker to almost any file. Keep `.zip` as the sole accept\\nvalue.\\n\\nCarbon does discard a file whose name fails its extension pattern, and\\nit passes nothing for a drop of non-file content, so `onAddFiles` can\\nreceive an empty list. Treat that like any other non-zip drop instead of\\nthrowing.\\n\\nuser-event applies the input's accept attribute by default, so the test\\nturns that off to exercise the component's own check.\\n\\n* Narrow the save error to OpenmrsFetchError and translate the fallback\\n\\nOnly an `OpenmrsFetchError` carries a response body, and only a JSON\\nbody carries the backend's reason. For anything else the old fallback\\nshowed the fetch error's own message, which tells the user to check\\n`err.responseBody` or the network tab. Show a translated generic message\\ninstead, matching the metadata export delete modal.\\n\\nThe failing-save test now rejects with a real `OpenmrsFetchError`.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T21:48:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack (#423)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack\\n\\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now put their fields in\\na Stack with gap={5}, and the form container sets the 16px padding.\\nBefore, each field set its own spacing: fixed heights with\\n30px bottom margins, an extra 50px margin and 32px top padding on the\\noutput format select, and 16px padding on each parameter and the cron\\neditor. That left uneven gaps between the fields.\\n\\nThe Report and Output format selects also lose their fixed 300px width,\\nso every field in both forms is full width like the parameter inputs.\\n\\n* Keep the cron editor's floated fields inside its wrapper\\n\\nThe schedule fields float, so the editor's wrapper only had a height\\nbecause the Stack around it is a grid. display: flow-root makes the\\nwrapper contain them in any parent.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T22:20:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Remove unused stylesheet classes from the reports app\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Delete 13 CSS Module classes in esm-reports-app that no component\\nreferences. Each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class only applies\\nwhen a file that imports that stylesheet uses it as styles.<name>, and\\nnone of these are:\\n\\n- root.scss: welcome, explainer (plus the @carbon/type import, which\\n  only welcome used)\\n- components/reports.scss: emptyButton, breadcrumbsSlot\\n- components/overlay.scss: closeButton, overlayContent (the desktop and\\n  tablet breakpoint blocks contained only overlayContent)\\n- components/run-report/run-report-form.scss: parameterElement,\\n  cancelActionButton, tableIcon, rowCellEven, rowCellOdd\\n- components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.scss:\\n  reportButton\\n- components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.scss: cronEditor\\n\\nrowCellEven, rowCellOdd and reportButton are still in use, but from\\nother stylesheets: the overview tables use the copies in reports.scss,\\nand the run report form uses the copy in run-report-form.scss. Only the\\nunreferenced duplicates are removed.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T21:08:13+03:00\",\"message\":\"chore: Remove inert Carbon CSS rules from reports app (#358)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"solomonfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3b89049a21f459607357c7704b11137465d948a1\",\"date\":\"2026-09-27T00:43:49+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5860: Add @carbon/react to peerDependencies (#324)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Declare @carbon/react as a 1.x peer in the OCL, patient documents admin, reports, system admin and metadata export apps, so the build tooling shares it with the app shell instead of bundling a separate copy.\",\"authorName\":\"Pankhudi_Singh\",\"authorEmail\":\"pankhudisingh121206@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"16972a9625452dceb98318d3b59d8e49eb68e935\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T01:55:13+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove nested anchors from the Legacy Admin and OCL admin cards\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Both cards wrapped ClickableTile in an outer anchor. ClickableTile\\nrenders its own anchor, so this produced invalid nested anchors and a\\ndead tab stop: keyboard users would focus the outer link, then land on\\nthe tile itself, which had tabindex 0 but no href and did nothing on\\nEnter.\\n\\nThe Legacy Admin card now passes href, target, and rel directly to\\nClickableTile, keeping its new tab behavior. Carbon's ClickableTileProps\\ntype omits target even though the component forwards extra props to the\\nunderlying anchor, so those props are passed via a spread.\\n\\nThe OCL card keeps its client-side same-tab navigation by calling\\nnavigate from an onClick handler for plain left clicks, mirroring what\\nConfigurableLink does. Modified clicks fall through to the anchor and\\nstill open a new tab or window.\\n\\nThe cardLink wrapper styles are no longer needed since there is no\\nouter anchor left to reset.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"39eb3196deef2ef9638b20e9333e2523a056a9e5\",\"date\":\"2025-04-29T12:09:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump @carbon/react to v1.76.0 (#76)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c47f18b3b3a9b6bc6ac972d74be977817c3bbf61\",\"date\":\"2022-08-24T12:25:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"BREAKING: Upgr